Our edits (re-apply after every refresh):
- vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/cli.rs: `#[derive(Parser, Debug, Default)]` on `Cli`
  so montage-cli can construct one programmatically. See crates/cli/src/chat_codex_cmd.rs.
- vendor/codex-rs/login/src/auth/default_client.rs,
  vendor/codex-rs/login/src/auth/manager.rs,
  vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/lib.rs,
  vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/event_processor_with_human_output.rs,
  vendor/codex-rs/analytics/src/events.rs, and
  vendor/codex-rs/model-provider-info/src/lib.rs:
  use each vendored crate's package version for model-manager, telemetry,
  display, and provider-version metadata. The login User-Agent may use
  `MONTAGE_CODEX_CLI_VERSION` when a deployment has sanctioned Codex backend
  access and must preserve the compatible Codex client version expected by the
  backend. Earlier Montage revisions hardcoded an installed Codex CLI version
  to bypass model-access gates; public source now requires explicit deployment
  configuration instead of silently mimicking another client.
  ChatGPT OAuth refresh/revoke read `MONTAGE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID`, the same
  sanctioned client id used by Montage's initial browser login flow, so public
  source does not embed another client's first-party id.
- vendor/codex-rs/models-manager/src/lib.rs: keep the Codex protocol/model
  discovery client version separate from Montage's workspace package version
  so `/models` filtering remains compatible with the vendored Codex engine.
- vendor/codex-rs/core/src/client.rs and vendor/codex-rs/core/src/turn_metadata.rs:
  keep Montage's current websocket metadata shape. Revisit this area when
  refreshing the fork against a sanctioned upstream client contract.
- vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/lib.rs: replace the hardcoded
  `approval_policy: Some(AskForApproval::Never)` in `ConfigOverrides`
  with a check that honors `config_toml.approval_policy` when the user
  has explicitly set one (via -c or config). Without this, `codex exec`
  unconditionally drops approvals in headless mode and per-tool MCP
  approval prompts never fire even when annotations and config say
  they should. Keeps `Never` as the default when the user hasn't set
  a policy, so existing non-interactive callers don't change behavior.
- vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/cli.rs and vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/lib.rs
  (fork patch #10): add `--base-instructions-file` and
  `--developer-instructions-file` flags to `codex exec`. When set, their
  file contents replace the hardcoded `base_instructions: None` /
  `developer_instructions: None` in `ConfigOverrides` (previously always
  `None`, i.e. stock `prompt.md` + no developer-tier override). Built for
  montage-eval's A/B harness (crates/eval/src/ab_driver.rs) so it can
  spawn `codex-exec` with Config A (stock prompt, flags omitted) or
  Config B (a merged base-prompt fixture + reduced developer instructions)
  as the single controlled variable — see
  docs/decision-prompt-layer-merge-2026-07-19.md §6/§8. Additive and
  reversible: omitting both flags is byte-for-byte identical to prior
  behavior (`None` default). Not used by any interactive/production Montage
  entry point today (agent-cli, codex-bridge) — only by the eval harness.
- vendor/codex-rs/tui/Cargo.toml + vendor/codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs:
  add `montage-proto = { workspace = true }` and `mod montage;` for the
  step-6 side panel.
- vendor/codex-rs/tui/src/montage/{mod,timeline,project_insights}.rs:
  new module hosting the Montage panel. Always-visible policy:
  uses `MONTAGE_PROJECT_ROOT` when set, otherwise falls back to
